{
  "hypothesis": {
    "id": "steer-decision-site-reachability-probe",
    "parent": "steer-steps-provenance-ablate",
    "kind": "enabling",
    "title": "Decide by unit test, not campaign, whether the steer decision site is reachable at all",
    "description": "Stop measuring the steer path with aggregate counters. In spur-core/tests/, add a direct test that drives the scheduler in-process over a handful of seeds of general_vr.json's grid arm for a bounded step count with a hook (test-only trait impl or a cfg(test) callback in spur-core/src/simulator/core/scheduler.rs) that records, per step, which of three outcomes occurred: (1) never entered the steer block, (2) entered but short-circuited before the express point (record the guard that returned early), (3) reached the express point. Assert the histogram is nonempty and print it. If outcome (3) is 0 across all seeds, the steerAuthority mechanism is dead code under this config and the entire preference/honored lineage should be closed rather than re-instrumented. If (2) dominates, the recorded guard names the single condition to target next.",
    "category": "tooling",
    "buildsOn": [
      "scheduler step loop",
      "util_stats",
      "util-stats-export-completeness-guard"
    ],
    "expectedGain": 4,
    "expectedCost": 1,
    "rationale": "preferenceExpressed has been exactly 0 over ~1.8e9 steps; the open question is no longer the size of the denominator but whether the numerator's code path executes. A deterministic in-process probe answers that in seconds and either kills a whole branch of the pool or hands back the exact early-return guard to attack.",
    "generalityArgument": "Instruments control-flow reachability inside the scheduler's own step loop and reports guard identities; makes no reference to VR, view changes, or any protocol-specific entity.",
    "status": "proposed",
    "branch": null,
    "prUrls": [],
    "createdAtIso": "2026-08-30T06:20:00Z",
    "firingCounter": null,
    "notes": "[unparked iteration 5358] Cheapest possible terminator for a family that has burned ~half of recent implement time; unit test decides reopen-or-close without a 300s campaign, given counters already show entry-then-short-circuit at source_absent."
  },
